From afb4abc52010f3d3347a8110a1af53171206562e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 08:40:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: opt-in explicit placement policy
 GGML_VK_PLACEMENT=bulk-large-heap (R46b commit E)

R47d (lane-232) traced both 27B S-X8 load failures to one mechanism, and it is a placement
mechanism, not an allocation-count or bounds one. ggml_vk_find_memory_properties tests each
allocation against the WHOLE heap size with no cumulative accounting, so GGML_VK_PREFER_HOST_MEMORY=1
lands the bulk weights on host-visible heap 1 and a 256 MiB grouping lands them in the small
combined-property heap 2 - and in BOTH arms the very first pinned 1 MiB upload then dies at
submit seq=0 with ErrorUnknown, after every allocation reported success. Allocation success does
not establish submit viability.

This adds the lever that lets that hypothesis be tested as a placement-only intervention.
GGML_VK_PLACEMENT=bulk-large-heap (exact string; anything else, including unset, changes nothing)
routes the bulk weight buffers - the grouped blocks the model loader suballocates tensors from -
to a DEVICE_LOCAL memory type on the LARGEST heap, and excludes every other heap for them. The
suballocation grouping is untouched, and staging, scratch and the prealloc buffers keep the paths
they use today. A refusal is not fatal: that one buffer falls through to the stock chain and says
so, because a policy that turns a working load into a hard failure is worse than the placement it
is trying to fix.

The receipt prints on stderr and is NOT gated on GGML_VK_ALLOC_TRACE - the paired performance
cells for this policy run with tracing off and still have to prove which heap the run used. Under
the trace, the existing alloc id=... state=try/ok lines already name the type and heap per buffer.

OWED, stated so it is not mistaken for done: the same commission asks for thread-safe cumulative
requirement reservations with rollback on failure and release on free, plus a bounded host split
with a declared staging reserve. This commit is heap SELECTION only. UNSCORED: the driver-internal
reason for ErrorUnknown. Proof cells A and B in PHASE-R46B.md are what would upgrade either.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
